settings-texture-gpu-memory = Active GPU memory capacity: { $mib } MiB (driver-reported capacity for shared-memory GPUs)
settings-texture-gpu-unknown = Capacity is unavailable for this GPU. Automatic mode uses a 512 MiB fallback within the GPU image size limit.
settings-texture-manual-range = Manual range: 1–{ $mib } MiB (this device's capacity, or its image size limit if capacity is unavailable)
settings-texture-resolved-budget = Image budget on this device: { $mib } MiB
settings-texture-limit = Maximum image edge on this device: { $edge } px (also limited by the GPU)
settings-texture-budget-hint = Lower percentages or budgets resize the image while keeping its aspect ratio and save GPU memory. Zoomed-in details become softer; piece sizes, positions, snapping and save data stay the same.
settings-texture-budget-scope = Covers the single shared RGBA8 image. The maximum edge also respects the game's 16384 px limit and the GPU limit, and fits a square within the budget. Increasing the budget may not improve an image's detail. This does not cap total GPU memory or decode CPU memory.
settings-texture-budget-next-load = Saved automatically and used for the next image selection or save load. The currently loaded image keeps its resolution.
